## 1. The Big Idea

_A working program is an assembly: atoms (24 joint movements) → molecules (6 compound patterns + isolation fillers) → variations (3–5 per pattern) → a Variation Cycle that rotates them on lifecycle. Standing orders (the 4 growth rules + 7 execution rules) govern how you operate the assembly. Lose either side and the program collapses._ The poster is an engineering reference card a lifter pins up beside the rack — a build sheet for the machine, with the standing orders running as a spec rail and the named failure modes printed below so they can't be forgotten.

