**LEFT RAIL — STANDING ORDERS**

**Panel A header:** `GROWTH RULES · what makes the stimulus work`

- `G·01 · ≥ 2× WEEKLY FREQUENCY PER MUSCLE` → `Once a week per muscle leaves growth on the table (Schoenfeld 2016). 3× vs 4× is murky — but 1× is the wrong floor.`
- `G·02 · 8–12 REPS × 2–3 SETS PER EXERCISE` → `Heavy enough for mechanical tension, light enough to push near failure without wrecking yourself. 3 sets on compounds, 2 on isolations.`
- `G·03 · DOUBLE PROGRESSION` → `Climb reps within the range at the same load; when the top of the range is hit on all sets, bump the load and drop back to the bottom. The data tells the truth — it can't be faked.`
- `G·04 · LAST SET TO HONEST FAILURE — form is the cue` → `The last 2–3 reps of the last set are where the growth signal actually lives. Failure = the rep where standardized form starts to break. Not heavy, not uncomfortable — broken.`

**Panel B header:** `EXECUTION RULES · what makes the program survive`

- `E·01 · NO STATIC STRETCHING PRE-LIFT` → `>60 s stretches cost 4–7.5% strength. Cascade up to working weight on the first exercise per muscle group instead (empty bar → 50% → 70% → 85% → working).`
- `E·02 · TRAIN INTENSITY, NOT VOLUME` → `Most lifters overestimate RIR by 2–4 reps. The "RIR 1" set is usually RIR 3. Calibrate by occasionally going to true mechanical failure.`
- `E·03 · 3 MIN REST BETWEEN WORKING SETS — non-negotiable` → `Less and the CNS can't recover; the next set falls short of true failure and the stimulus per set is degraded. Phone-scrolling is fine; cutting rest to "save time" is sabotage.`
- `E·04 · SORENESS IS NOT A GROWTH SIGNAL` → `DOMS is a marker of unaccustomed eccentric stress, not training quality. A muscle that isn't sore can absolutely be growing. Damage ≠ stimulus.`
- `E·05 · DON'T PROGRAM-HOP — commit 8–12 weeks` → `Switching exercises every 2–3 weeks resets the neural adaptation curve constantly. The muscles aren't guessing; they're learning. Learning takes time.`
- `E·06 · TRACK EVERY SET — Hevy or equivalent` → `Double progression is impossible without an accurate record of last session. Memory isn't reliable at the precision the program needs.`
- `E·07 · PROGRESS PICS WEEKLY · FORM-CHECK VIDEOS EVERY 4–6 WK` → `The mirror lies; pictures don't. Form drift caught on video is the catch for fake progressive overload. If bar path or depth shifted, the muscle being trained has shifted with it.`

